# indyr4400 station.env fixture — appended to the emitted station.env, and the
# SINGLE source for every key it defines (the registry entry must not repeat
# one; the validator fails the gate if it does).
#
# HOST-NATIVE since the 2026-09 de-bridging (docs/lab/IRIS-DEBRIDGE-BRIEF.md,
# ledger in docs/lab/IRIS-DEBRIDGE-LEDGER.md). Iris — the userspace Rust SGI
# Indy emulator, github.com/Wnt/iris — runs on the host inside a systemd-nspawn
# container with NO X, NO window and NO QEMU, and publishes its own planes:
# IFB1 frames to SH_SHM_PATH and mamectl/1 input on SH_MAMECTL_SOCK. streamhost
# consumes both with env alone; not a line of daemon code is new here.
# Launcher: stations/indyr4400/x11-runtime.sh (+ nspawn-inner.sh, PID 2 inside).
#
# WHY: one pointer move took 361 ms to reach the framebuffer on the bridge and
# 68 ms on the host-native MAME `irix` sibling. The lag was QEMU PS/2 -> guest
# X -> winit -> llvmpipe -> dbus, not the emulator core. Every one of those is
# gone.

# ---- FRAMES ----------------------------------------------------------------
# SH_SHM_DAMAGE IS LEFT AT THE DAEMON'S DEFAULT (on), and the `nextstep`
# precedent for setting it to 0 does not survive reading the daemon. Checked
# against streamhost/src/capture/shm.rs and config/mod.rs this session: the shm
# backend NEVER reads the header's dirty rect. All it takes from the header is
# "changed or not"; `SH_SHM_DAMAGE=1` then diffs the copy against the previous
# frame to recover a sub-frame bbox for the encoder, and `SH_SHM_DAMAGE=0` marks
# every dirty frame FULL-FRAME as the A/B control. So 0 does not mean "trust the
# producer's rect", it means "throw sub-frame damage away" — the wrong side of
# the trade on a 1280x1024x4 desktop where the usual delta is a cursor.
#
# What the producer's own rect DOES buy is upstream of the daemon: the fork
# publishes only CHANGED frames (`damage=derived` in the launch log, its
# IRIS_SHM_DAMAGE knob), so an idle Indy copies nothing at all. That saving is
# independent of this line.

# ---- INPUT: mamectl/1, absolute pointer, per-station keymap ----------------
# SH_MAMESOCK_KEYMAP is stream C's file (winit KeyCode names on port `kbd`, the
# nextstep.keymap shape). The launcher REFUSES to start in shm mode without it:
# a missing keymap is a silently dead keyboard, which is the failure mode this
# station already shipped once (the winit focus trap on the bridge).
SH_MAMECTL_SOCK=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/indyr4400/run/ctl.sock
SH_MAMESOCK_KEYMAP=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/indyr4400/indy.keymap
# SH_MAMESOCK_PTR_GRID stays UNSET: this server states targets in screen pixels.
#
# Iris samples input once per emulated frame and every key here is synthetic, so
# pace press/release at the fleet floor derived from the emulated 60 Hz refresh
# — the value the bridge measured and shipped. Retune from a real ctlsock trace
# with a PIPELINED sender (scripts/dev/key-replay.py); an acking client paces
# the edges for you and hides the bug perfectly.
SH_KEY_MIN_HOLD_MS=40
SH_KEY_MIN_GAP_MS=40
# A conservative starting floor, NOT a measurement: stream C sweeps it against
# IRIX's own double-click verdict the way nextstep did.
SH_BTN_MIN_HOLD_MS=60

# ---- RESET -----------------------------------------------------------------
# relaunch -> `systemctl restart streamhost@indyr4400` -> ExecStartPre ->
# x11-runtime.sh, which kills the container, wipes work/ and restores
# IRIS_STATE in-process (Iris's own ci_rollback, ~42 ms on its CHANGELOG).
# IRIS_STATE empty forces a cold boot (~7 min: PROM, IRIX autoconfig relink,
# login), exactly as IRIX_STATE= does on the `irix` sibling — the bounded
# fallback, and a visibly degraded exhibit while it runs.
SH_RESET_MODE=relaunch
SH_FIXTURE_DESC=SGI Indy (MIPS R4400, 256 MB, XL 24-bit) IRIX 6.5.22 on the Indigo Magic Desktop (4Dwm, demos session: Toolchest docked upper-left, the camera/Start Demos/buttonfly/fsn icon column down the right edge), drawn by Iris HOST-NATIVE at 1280x1024 with no window, no X server and no kiosk. Iris's own 16-row status HUD is a separate GL texture and cannot enter the published frame, so the X-root clipping the bridge needed is gone with it.

# ---- STANDBY ---------------------------------------------------------------
# A non-QEMU station gets idle auto-pause ONLY if its env names the emulator's
# pidfile: idle.rs never infers a freezer. Without these three keys Iris — the
# most expensive emulator in the lineup, ~320-360 % CPU — burns cores forever.
# The proc match is scoped to THIS station's own asset path.
#
# DELIBERATELY NO SH_IDLE_PAUSE_SECS OVERRIDE. This station takes the fleet
# default; never copy the amiga/gt40/irix SH_IDLE_PAUSE_SECS=0 stanza onto it.
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PIDFILE=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/indyr4400/mame.pid
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PROC_MATCH=assets/indyr4400/iris
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_WARMUP_SECS=120

# ---- EMULATOR (read by x11-runtime.sh, not by the daemon) ------------------
IRIS_ASSETS=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/indyr4400
IRIS_BIN=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/indyr4400/iris
IRIS_DISK=/data/gallery-guests/IrisIndy/irix65-r4400-disk.raw
IRIS_GEOM=1280x1024
IRIS_CI_SOCK=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/indyr4400/run/iris-ci.sock
IRIS_STATE=golden
# vc2 arms stream C's CLOSED absolute loop against Iris's own VC2 hardware-cursor
# registers — the same pointer+31-hotspot arithmetic the MAME `irix` sibling
# already runs against this same IRIX 6.5 X server, and the reason it converges
# is that IRIX's acceleration is 1:1 near zero. This string is also the device
# ledger token scripts/stations_registry/pointer_rules.py requires for the
# declared pointer method: the registry cannot claim an absolute pointer that
# the launcher does not arm.
IRIS_PTR_MODE=vc2
# Multiple of 65536, claimed through kh-claim; medley=1966080, lisa=200000.
IRIS_UID_BASE=2031616
IRIS_STANDBY_DELAY_S=120
